  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>The Clappertons were drapers in <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> for twenty-four years, from 1857 to 1880. A. and G. Clapperton, drapers, are listed in 1857 and 1858, and Adam and Geo. Clapperton, drapers, at No. 33 in 1859 and Nos 35 and 37 in 1860 and 1861. From 1862 to 1880 the business is G. or George Clapperton, draper, at Nos 35 and 37 (No. 35 in 1869, and no number given from 1870 to 1873). From 1864 it is the first listing after the Ballarat Street corner.</p>
        <p>A William Clapperton is listed beside the drapers in 1857, and W. or William Clapperton, store, later grocer, at the corner of Bouverie and Queensberry streets from 1864 to 1868. Those listings are not linked to this entry.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>Copley and Son, basket makers, are next door in 1862 and 1863. From 1862 to 1877 the bootmaker J. or John Lanigan is at Nos 31 and 33 (Charles Lanigan from 1872 to 1874), followed by R. or Richard Prittie, bootmaker, from 1878. In 1885 the grocer <ref target="civic?id=William%20Norris">William Norris</ref> is listed at Nos 35 and 37.</p>
      </div>
